The weighted average cost per unit for the period is  

\[
\text{Weighted average cost} = \frac{\text{Total cost of goods available}}{\text{Total units available}}
= \frac{1250 + 116 + 440}{200 + 20 + 80}
= \frac{1806}{300}
= \$6.02 \text{ per unit}
\]

Cobb sold 10 units, so the cost of goods sold is  

\[
10 \times 6.02 = \$60.20
\]

**ANSWER: A**
